  "verificationScope": "# Original Lemma4.2: continuation under an UNVERIFIED canonical input\n\nOriginal Lemma4.1, original Lemma4.2 and the final Linearity Theorem remain OPEN.\nThe user authorized continuing under the genuine canonical identification as an\nexplicit unverified hypothesis. No new axiom or proof placeholder is used.\nThis is an independent local component, not a whole-project checkpoint or CI.\n\nLet D be an actual native module sheaf, T_m actual twists, and assume an explicit\nnative embedding into one positive m. Given an explicit F ~= D, composition\ntransfers that embedding to F. The SAME m is chosen before F and the identification.\nThis generic implication is proved. The canonical/normalized-dualizing identity\nis not proved; the large-type original-Proj specialization failed and is excluded.\n\nLet j:F -> T be an actual module-sheaf monomorphism. Then it is injective on\nsections over every open. A nonzero section stays nonzero. For every actual\nsubscheme pullback i, i*(s)=0 implies i*(j(s))=0, using the actual pullback functor.\nInjectivity on residue fibres is NOT asserted. No flatness hypothesis is hidden.\n\nA homogeneous element ell defines the actual global local-fraction section ell/1\non Proj, with its actual value formula and zero/nonzero tests. For the ORIGINAL\nintegral projective equations V over C, a homogeneous Q gives Q-bar/1 in the actual\nnative positive local-fraction twist T_m. A nonzero such section implies Q not in\nV's ORIGINAL defining ideal. For the SAME original V, if j(a)=Q-bar/1 and a is\nnonzero, then Q is not in I(V). Existence of this polynomial lift is still OPEN.\n\nActual library reuse: SheafCohomologySectionSurjectivity adapts the argument in\nCBirkbeck/AINTLIB, commit ab1451487da02cd4483d0e2cdb2cc9e44bbbac17,\nModularCurves/ForMathlib/SheafCohomologyExact.lean. For an ACTUAL short exact\nsequence of additive sheaves 0 -> A -> B -> C -> 0, H^1(A)=0 implies B(T)->C(T)\nis surjective at the terminal object, using mathlib's actual long exact sequence.\nThis precise implication was compiled/audited in Linear's pinned mathlib.\nIt is NOT the eventual Serre vanishing theorem. Apache 2.0 attribution is retained.\n\nSix new canonical LF modules: 16 proofs, 2 definitions, 18 exact declaration/axiom\naudits accepted. All other 93 project dependencies match checkpoint180 byte for\nbyte. The 99-module closed source and five reproducibility files are included;\nLinear.lean is only an import entry, not separately compiled. Compiler logs,\nresource records, actual exact types and axioms are included. Only propext,\nClassical.choice and Quot.sound occur. One compiler, 8 GiB hard Windows Job,\n2 threads, CPU25%, below normal, 20-minute timeout. Accepted audit peak 4.24 GiB.\n\nRemaining original obligations: genuine canonical/normalized-dualizing identity;\nconcrete original-Proj specialization; Koszul/proper-duality production of a!=0\nwith the required vanishing; eventual Serre bound and actual homogeneous polynomial\nlifting in ONE degree independent of the iterate. AINTLIB eventual-Cech-vanishing\ncode was located and its 157-file source closure reviewed, but it has unrelated\nupstream placeholders and a different mathlib pin. That foreign closure is NOT\nincluded or counted as verified. The next step extracts minimal generic proofs.\nWhole-project checkpoint180 and all original open statuses are unchanged.\n",
